From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 08:23:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: store the queue masks when the iOS driver drained
 events

On iOS process_driver_events calls winios.drv's pProcessEvents on every
thread and sends set_queue_mask with poll_events set when it drained
input. No iOS queue has a driver fd (nothing sends set_queue_fd), and the
server's set_queue_mask returns before it stores the wake and changed
masks when poll_events is set and the queue has no fd. A thread about to
wait in MsgWaitForMultipleObjects whose call drained input (gyro or
touch input, which reaches dinput's worker as raw input) kept the masks
an earlier call left, possibly none: a message then sent to it never
woke it, and the sender waited for ever. The Witcher 3 hung at quit this
way: its main thread's SendMessage of dinput's NOTIFY_REFRESH_DEVICES to
wine_dinput_worker ("[sendmsg-stuck] ... msg=410 ... to tid=00b4").

poll_events is now never set on iOS; the masks are always stored.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-14-witcher3-quit-hang.md
Offered-upstream: no; winios.drv and the always-on pProcessEvents are Madeira's
---
 build/win32u-unix/message_ios.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/win32u-unix/message_ios.c b/build/win32u-unix/message_ios.c
index 0bb248f..74a440d 100644
--- a/build/win32u-unix/message_ios.c
+++ b/build/win32u-unix/message_ios.c
@@ -3431,7 +3431,18 @@ static BOOL process_driver_events( UINT events_mask, UINT wake_mask, UINT change
 #endif
         if (!skip_server) SERVER_START_REQ( set_queue_mask )
         {
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+            /* iOS: pProcessEvents drains winios.drv's ring on any thread and
+             * no queue on iOS has a driver fd (nothing sends set_queue_fd).
+             * The server's set_queue_mask returns early when poll_events is
+             * set and the queue has no fd, without storing the masks below;
+             * a thread that then waits in MsgWaitForMultipleObjects (Wine's
+             * dinput worker) is never woken by a sent message, and its
+             * sender hangs (The Witcher 3 at quit, PLA-344). */
+            req->poll_events = 0;
+#else
             req->poll_events = drained;
+#endif
             req->wake_mask = wake_mask;
             req->changed_mask = changed_mask;
             wine_server_call( req );
